<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    JWT/JWS verification, compact serialization (header.payload.signature).
    Runs when signature.verify.type = "jwt" AND
    signature.verify.jwt.detached != "true" (see the -Detached sibling
    for that case).

    Native VerifyJWS — no custom crypto needed, unlike Cavage/XML-DSig.
    KeyStore/Alias are per-proxy, resolved at runtime from this proxy's
    KVM config (see EV-JWT-Verify-Parse-Config) via ref, the same
    ref-to-a-flow-variable pattern ServiceCallout/TargetEndpoint use for
    <SSLInfo><KeyStore ref="...">.

    continueOnError defaults to false, so an invalid/expired/malformed
    JWS raises a policy fault here and the request is rejected; nothing
    else needs to check a "valid" flag. Add a FaultRule if you want a
    response shape other than Apigee's default JWS-fault response.

    Algorithm AND KnownHeaders are pinned here deliberately rather than
    KVM-sourced, for the same reason: both are security-relevant
    allow-lists (accepted signing algorithm; extension header params
    this proxy claims to understand for RFC 7515 §4.1.11's "crit"
    check), so they belong in a reviewed policy change, not
    config anyone with KVM write access could alter — same reasoning
    IgnoreCriticalHeaders stays "false": accepting a JWS whose "crit"
    lists something outside KnownHeaders should fail closed, not be
    toggled off by config. x-txn-id is this proxy's one custom
    extension (see examples/kvm/orders-api.signature.jwt-header.json on
    the signing side). If more than one algorithm or extension header
    is genuinely needed, add more <Algorithm>/<Header> entries here —
    don't make either fully dynamic. A different proxy needing a
    different KnownHeaders list gets its own copy of this policy pair
    (same reasoning as SF-SAML-Extractor's per-proxy profiles).

    UNVERIFIED: I can't check the exact <KnownHeaders>/<Header> child
    element shape against Apigee's reference docs from here — if it
    turns out to be a different structure (e.g. a single
    comma-separated value, or repeated <KnownHeader> without a
    wrapper), adjust this policy; nothing else in the shared flow
    depends on its internals.
-->
<VerifyJWS name="VerifyJWS-Jwt-Compact" continueOnError="false">
    <DisplayName>VerifyJWS-Jwt-Compact</DisplayName>
    <Algorithm>RS256</Algorithm>
    <Source>signature.verify.jwt.jws</Source>
    <PublicKey>
        <KeyStore ref="signature.verify.jwt.keystore.name"/>
        <Alias ref="signature.verify.jwt.keystore.alias"/>
    </PublicKey>
    <KnownHeaders>
        <Header>x-txn-id</Header>
    </KnownHeaders>
    <IgnoreCriticalHeaders>false</IgnoreCriticalHeaders>
    <VariablePrefix>signature.verify.jwt</VariablePrefix>
</VerifyJWS>
